\title{plotly: interactive web graphics with plot_ly() and ggplotly()}
\description{
plotly builds interactive plots with \code{\link[=plot_ly]{plot_ly()}} and \code{\link[=ggplotly]{ggplotly()}}. Plots
are rendered by the plotly.core package, which bundles plotly.js and
provides the widget, Shiny integration and static image export, along
with graph objects (\verb{go_*()}) and Plotly Express (\verb{px_*()}) interfaces.
A \code{plot_ly()} object can be turned into a plotly.core figure with
\code{\link[=legacy_figure]{legacy_figure()}}.
